      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 S. Karger AG, Basel.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Surgical resection of craniopharyngiomas may be challenging sometimes because of the size, location and tenacity. Simultaneous endoscopic and microsurgical resection is a novel way to approach such lesions. The aim of this report is to discuss the usefulness of combined endoscopic and microsurgical approaches in treating complex craniopharyngiomas along with a review of the literature."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "A child with hydrocephalus and a large suprasellar craniopharyngioma underwent synchronous endoscopic and microsurgical resection of the lesion."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Gross total resection of the tumor was achieved. There were no postoperative complications. Hydrocephalus was also treated successfully."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "Neuroendoscopy can complement microsurgery in approaching complex craniopharyngiomas particularly when these tumors are large and accompanied by hydrocephalus."
          }
        ]
      },
